WEBVTT

00:00.990 --> 00:06.930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

00:00.990 --> 00:06.930
Just like the cruel angel

00:06.930 --> 00:14.590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

00:06.930 --> 00:14.590
Young boy, become a legend

00:18.990 --> 00:22.410
2D4U PRESENTS:

00:22.770 --> 00:25.810
Aoi kaze ga ima

00:22.770 --> 00:25.810
Even though the untested breeze...

00:25.810 --> 00:29.510
mune no doa o tataitemo

00:25.810 --> 00:29.510
...taps at the door to your heart

00:29.510 --> 00:36.970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

00:29.510 --> 00:36.970
You just look solely at me and smile

00:37.560 --> 00:44.500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

00:37.560 --> 00:44.500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

00:44.500 --> 00:51.400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

00:44.500 --> 00:51.400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

00:52.000 --> 00:55.750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

00:52.000 --> 00:55.750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

00:55.750 --> 00:58.340
sono senaka ni wa

00:55.750 --> 00:58.340
...that upon your back

00:59.510 --> 01:02.960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

00:59.510 --> 01:02.960
You have the wings with which to fly...

01:02.960 --> 01:06.310
no hane ga aru koto

01:02.960 --> 01:06.310
...towards the distant future

01:06.990 --> 01:10.690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

01:06.990 --> 01:10.690
The cruel angel's thesis

01:10.690 --> 01:14.430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

01:10.690 --> 01:14.430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

01:14.430 --> 01:18.200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

01:14.430 --> 01:18.200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

01:18.200 --> 01:21.900
Omoide o uragiru nara

01:18.200 --> 01:21.900
If you are to betray our memories

01:21.900 --> 01:25.540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

01:21.900 --> 01:25.540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

01:25.540 --> 01:29.270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

01:25.540 --> 01:29.270
Young boy, become a legend

01:31.610 --> 01:33.990
Once again, I owe you.

01:33.990 --> 01:36.200
You're not going to pay me
back anyway, are you?

01:36.200 --> 01:39.870
About the materials they wanted under
Freedom of Information,

01:39.490 --> 01:42.290
First Interim Report Concerning
Objects Referred to as Angels
and the Human Instrumentality Project

01:39.870 --> 01:42.660
I handled it by giving them
some falsified data.

01:42.660 --> 01:45.330
The government is quietly
pursuing legal action,

01:45.330 --> 01:47.420
but that will be blocked any day now.

01:47.420 --> 01:52.130
So, should I do something about
that project as well?

01:52.130 --> 01:55.550
No, judging by the material you sent me,
there should be no problem.

01:55.550 --> 01:57.630
Then, I'll continue as planned.

01:57.680 --> 02:00.390
EPISODE 07
THAT WHICH
IS MANMADE

02:10.400 --> 02:12.270
Good morning.

02:15.940 --> 02:16.570
G'morning.

02:26.120 --> 02:28.870
This is the way to start your morning!

02:28.870 --> 02:30.630
Not with coffee?

02:30.630 --> 02:37.550
A traditional Japanese breakfast begins
with rice, miso, and sake.

02:37.550 --> 02:39.550
You mean YOUR traditional breakfast.

02:39.550 --> 02:41.220
What's that supposed to mean?

02:41.220 --> 02:45.390
Besides, who was supposed
to cook this morning anyway?

02:45.390 --> 02:50.270
Now I know why you're still single
at your age, Miss Misato.

02:50.270 --> 02:52.810
Well, excuse me for being coarse.

02:52.810 --> 02:54.610
And sloppy too.

02:54.610 --> 02:57.110
Leave me alone!

02:57.110 --> 02:57.860
I'm done.

03:00.450 --> 03:02.660
Are you really going to come
to school today?

03:02.660 --> 03:06.080
Of course. It's your parent-teacher
meeting after all.

03:06.080 --> 03:07.950
But you're so busy with your work.

03:07.950 --> 03:11.250
Don't worry about it. This is
part of my job too.

03:11.250 --> 03:12.710
It's part of your job?

03:16.210 --> 03:18.050
Yes?

03:18.050 --> 03:22.550
Oh, thanks for coming all this way!
Yes, wait just a minute.

03:22.550 --> 03:25.560
Miss Misato, please don't go out like that.

03:25.560 --> 03:27.100
It's embarrassing.

03:27.100 --> 03:28.020
Okay, okay.

03:31.390 --> 03:33.480
Good morning, Ikari!

03:33.480 --> 03:35.940
We're taking off now, Miss Misato!

03:35.940 --> 03:37.190
See you!

03:39.360 --> 03:40.610
Let's get going!

03:45.280 --> 03:46.950
Ah, sarcasm.

03:46.950 --> 03:50.960
Well, I guess it's good that he's loosening up
and expressing himself more.

03:56.170 --> 03:57.130
Yes?

03:57.130 --> 04:00.130
He just left. I'll leave guarding him
from here to you.

04:12.690 --> 04:14.270
She's arrived!

04:20.280 --> 04:22.110
Cool! Who is she?

04:22.110 --> 04:23.320
Ikari's guardian?

04:23.320 --> 04:26.660
What?! He's got a babe like that
for a guardian?!

04:26.660 --> 04:27.330
They're such dorks.

04:29.660 --> 04:33.210
Miss Misato really is awesome!

04:33.210 --> 04:34.370
You think so?

04:34.370 --> 04:37.920
It's even more amazin' that she's
Nerv's Ops Director.

04:37.920 --> 04:39.380
You think so?

04:40.170 --> 04:44.680
It's just a counseling session but
my mother had to dress up!

04:40.800 --> 04:43.760
Good thing that Shinji's
such a baby, Kensuke.

04:43.760 --> 04:46.640
Yeah, Shinji's no rival for us!

04:44.680 --> 04:46.640
Don't you think she's silly?

04:46.640 --> 04:50.180
You guys don't know what a slob she is.

04:50.180 --> 04:54.100
Man, I wish I had a girlfriend like her!

04:54.100 --> 04:56.150
I bet you'd have a tough time.

04:56.150 --> 04:58.110
You just don't get it, do you, Mr. Big Shot?

04:58.110 --> 05:01.280
All right, we'll leave protecting
the Earth to you,

05:01.280 --> 05:03.610
so you leave Miss Misato to us!

05:06.110 --> 05:08.620
Unit 01 has achieved the
required cooling level.

05:08.620 --> 05:10.990
Please shift operations to Stage 2.

05:09.530 --> 05:11.870
Protecting the Earth...

05:11.870 --> 05:13.040
That's what Eva is for.

05:14.370 --> 05:16.540
Come to think of it, just what is the Eva?

05:16.540 --> 05:18.750
The entry plug smells like blood.

05:18.750 --> 05:21.550
But I feel so relaxed here. Why?

05:22.550 --> 05:25.760
In the end, I don't know anything.

05:26.470 --> 05:29.220
What's the status of Unit 00's
bio-chest components?

05:29.220 --> 05:30.930
It was seriously damaged.

05:30.930 --> 05:34.430
We'll make a new one, but it'll barely fit
within our supplementary budget.

05:34.430 --> 05:38.560
Will our job get any simpler once
we get Unit 02 from Germany?

05:38.560 --> 05:40.230
It could go the other way.

05:40.230 --> 05:43.190
Disposing of the Angel on the surface
isn't cheap, right?

05:43.190 --> 05:46.280
Yeah, this place is really tight
when it comes to money.

05:46.280 --> 05:48.570
We're talking about the fate of mankind here!

05:48.570 --> 05:49.990
It can't be helped.

05:49.990 --> 05:52.240
"Man cannot live by Eva alone."

05:52.240 --> 05:55.370
All those survivors need money to live too.

05:55.370 --> 05:56.830
Budgets...

05:56.830 --> 05:58.580
So, is the Commander off
to another conference?

05:58.580 --> 06:01.130
Yes, he's on the plane now.

06:01.130 --> 06:04.050
It's nice and quiet here
when he's not around.

06:11.720 --> 06:15.560
Excuse me. Since we're sharing the flight,
do you mind if I sit here?

06:17.520 --> 06:19.940
The revised budget for the sample collection

06:19.940 --> 06:21.770
passed quite easily, didn't it?

06:21.770 --> 06:25.570
The Committee's main concern
is for their own survival.

06:25.570 --> 06:27.700
They aren't stingy when their
own lives are at stake.

06:27.700 --> 06:31.530
After all, the basis of their argument was
that no more Angels would appear.

06:31.530 --> 06:33.950
Oh, I have one more piece of good news.

06:33.950 --> 06:39.290
All members of the UN except the U.S.
have approved the budget for Eva Unit 06.

06:39.290 --> 06:42.630
Well, it's probably just a matter of time
for the U.S. as well.

06:42.630 --> 06:46.800
That country is allergic
to unemployment, after all.

06:46.800 --> 06:48.130
And what about your country?

06:48.130 --> 06:50.430
We will participate beginning with
the construction of Unit 08.

06:50.430 --> 06:53.720
The plans for the second installation
project are still viable.

06:53.720 --> 06:57.980
However, there is the problem of
not yet having found a pilot.

06:57.980 --> 07:00.810
The Angels have appeared once again.

07:00.810 --> 07:03.940
We have no choice but to defeat them.

07:03.940 --> 07:08.440
We don't want another
Second Impact either.

07:08.440 --> 07:13.370
Then you're saying that the Second Impact
that evaporated Antarctica wasn't...

07:13.370 --> 07:18.700
Yes, the history texts say it was
a disaster caused by a huge meteorite,

07:18.410 --> 07:23.380
Giant Explosion at the South Pole

07:18.700 --> 07:21.870
but sometimes the truth
has been covered up.

07:21.870 --> 07:23.960
Fifteen years ago at the South Pole,

07:23.960 --> 07:28.300
mankind discovered the humanoid being
known as the first "Angel".

07:28.300 --> 07:29.720
However, in the middle of the investigation,

07:29.720 --> 07:32.840
for reasons unknown,
there was a huge explosion.

07:32.840 --> 07:35.600
That is the real truth behind
the Second Impact.

07:35.600 --> 07:38.060
Then, what we're doing here...

07:38.060 --> 07:41.350
To prevent a probable Third Impact
from happening.

07:41.350 --> 07:44.560
That is the purpose of Nerv
and the Evangelions.

07:45.360 --> 07:48.070
By the way, the event will occur
tomorrow as scheduled.

07:49.940 --> 07:50.860
I understand.

08:04.000 --> 08:05.540
Good morning.

08:05.540 --> 08:07.380
Good morning.

08:07.380 --> 08:10.050
I'm going to Old Tokyo on business.

08:10.050 --> 08:13.220
I'll probably be back late tonight,
so have delivery for dinner.

08:13.220 --> 08:14.390
Later.

08:15.340 --> 08:17.050
Okay.

08:22.810 --> 08:26.520
Abandoned Zone 28 (Center of Old Tokyo)

08:31.150 --> 08:35.610
It's hard to believe this used to be
the flourishing capital of Tokyo.

08:35.610 --> 08:37.120
We're here.

08:38.080 --> 08:41.790
Of all places, they didn't have to hold it here.

08:41.790 --> 08:44.580
So, is the SSDF involved in this project?

08:44.580 --> 08:48.540
The Strategic Self Defense Force?
No, they're not allowed to interfere.

08:48.540 --> 08:50.380
No wonder they're doing as they please.

08:57.800 --> 09:01.220
Celebrating JA Completion
Announcement Commemoration

08:58.550 --> 09:01.220
Thank you very much for taking the time
out of your busy schedules today

09:01.220 --> 09:05.140
Nerv Party

09:01.220 --> 09:05.140
to attend the demonstration
of the new product

09:05.140 --> 09:07.980
that we at Japan Heavy Chemical Industries
are so proud of.

09:08.940 --> 09:14.400
Later, you will be observing the offical
demonstration from the control room,

09:14.400 --> 09:17.200
but we'll be taking your questions here.

09:17.200 --> 09:17.780
Yes!

09:17.780 --> 09:20.990
The famous Dr. Ritsuko Akagi.

09:20.990 --> 09:23.160
It is our honor to have you here.

09:23.160 --> 09:25.410
May I ask a question?

09:25.410 --> 09:27.330
Of course, certainly!

09:27.330 --> 09:29.000
According to our earlier briefing,

09:29.000 --> 09:31.050
this unit is equipped with an
internal nuclear reactor, correct?

09:31.050 --> 09:33.800
Yes, this is one of our product's
most distinguished features.

09:33.800 --> 09:38.010
150 days of consecutive
operating power is assured.

09:38.010 --> 09:42.770
But from a safety perspective, isn't
incorporating a nuclear reactor

09:42.770 --> 09:46.350
into a weapon designed for
hand-to-hand combat risky?

09:46.350 --> 09:50.360
It's better than a weapon that
won't work for over five minutes.

09:50.360 --> 09:53.530
But in an emergency there could be
problems with remote control.

09:53.530 --> 09:55.070
Still it's more humane than a system

09:55.070 --> 09:59.030
that induces great mental stress,
and causes mental instability.

09:59.030 --> 10:01.280
Cut it out. This just makes
you look childish.

10:01.280 --> 10:03.240
And there's still the issue of manual control.

10:03.240 --> 10:07.540
I believe that it is safer than a most
dangerous weapon

10:07.540 --> 10:09.380
that can go out of control and run wild.

10:09.380 --> 10:12.380
A weapon that cannot be controlled
is utter nonsense!

10:12.380 --> 10:15.510
It's like a woman in hysterics!

10:15.510 --> 10:17.090
Unmanageable!

10:19.550 --> 10:22.100
That is what our pilots
and technology are for.

10:22.100 --> 10:26.600
You're not saying that science and the
human heart will tame that beast?

10:26.600 --> 10:27.850
Are you serious?

10:27.850 --> 10:29.650
Yes, of course I'm serious!

10:29.650 --> 10:32.520
Because Nerv depends on something
as unreliable as the human heart,

10:32.520 --> 10:35.400
you've allowed a loss of control
such as we just saw.

10:35.400 --> 10:38.900
That's why the UN had to approve
that colossal supplementary budget.

10:38.900 --> 10:42.450
As a result, over 20,000 people
in several countries are starving.

10:42.450 --> 10:44.990
On top of which, regardless of it having been
such a critical incident,

10:44.990 --> 10:47.540
the causes of it are still unknown?

10:47.540 --> 10:51.290
I wish you would at least fulfill that much
of your responsibilities!

10:51.290 --> 10:58.170
I envy you. Nerv is protected by a super-legal
act that allows you to avoid responsibility.

10:58.170 --> 10:59.720
It doesn't matter what you say.

10:59.720 --> 11:03.220
The fact is that only Nerv's weapons have
the ability to defeat the enemy.

11:03.220 --> 11:05.220
You mean the AT field?

11:05.220 --> 11:07.850
That's just a matter of time as well.

11:07.850 --> 11:10.440
Nerv's day in the sun will not last forever.

11:12.650 --> 11:13.980
Nerv Party

11:14.980 --> 11:20.360
Damn it! Idiots! Who do those
fat cats think they are?!

11:20.360 --> 11:24.070
This is just payback for getting
cut out of the profit loop!

11:24.070 --> 11:26.790
I am so pissed!

11:26.790 --> 11:28.330
Damn it! Damn it!

11:28.330 --> 11:30.920
Stop that. This just makes you look childish.

11:30.920 --> 11:34.000
He's just a show-off, begging for praise.

11:34.000 --> 11:36.300
He's a small man.

11:36.300 --> 11:39.420
But how did he even know
about the AT field?!

11:39.420 --> 11:41.300
There's been a huge leak
of classified material.

11:41.300 --> 11:43.220
What the hell is Intelligence doing?

11:56.520 --> 11:59.740
We will now begin the JA activation test.

12:00.190 --> 12:02.200
There is absolutely no danger.

12:02.990 --> 12:05.740
Make yourselves comfortable,
and watch through that window.

12:07.580 --> 12:09.120
Ready to activate.

12:09.120 --> 12:10.290
Start the test.

12:10.290 --> 12:11.620
Open all power circuits.

12:11.620 --> 12:13.330
Pressure levels nominal.

12:13.330 --> 12:15.040
Coolant system circulation nominal.

12:15.040 --> 12:16.840
Release the control rods.

12:16.840 --> 12:18.840
The reactor has exceeded threshold levels.

12:18.840 --> 12:20.630
Output is nominal.

12:20.630 --> 12:21.880
Begin walk cycle!

12:21.880 --> 12:24.390
Walking. Forward ahead, slow.
Forward right leg.

12:24.390 --> 12:26.930
Roger. Walk, forward ahead slow.

12:26.470 --> 12:28.010
Forward

12:26.470 --> 12:28.010
Stop

12:26.470 --> 12:28.010
Reverse

12:26.470 --> 12:28.010
Slow

12:26.470 --> 12:28.010
Half
Speed

12:26.470 --> 12:28.010

 Normal

12:26.470 --> 12:28.010
Flank
Speed

12:26.930 --> 12:28.010
Forward right leg.

12:33.890 --> 12:35.060
Balance is nominal.

12:35.060 --> 12:36.480
Power core status nominal.

12:36.480 --> 12:37.400
Roger.

12:37.400 --> 12:39.320
Now, forward left leg.

12:39.320 --> 12:40.400
Keep her steady.

12:43.070 --> 12:47.070
It actually walks! I guess they did have
something to be proud of.

12:49.870 --> 12:51.580
What's wrong?

12:50.540 --> 12:54.160
This is odd. The pressure inside
the reactor is increasing.

12:54.160 --> 12:56.960
The temperature of the primary coolant
system is also rising!

12:56.960 --> 12:58.210
Open the release valve.

12:58.210 --> 12:59.630
Insert the neutron-deceleration fluid.

12:59.630 --> 13:00.550
No effect!

13:00.550 --> 13:02.210
The pump output isn't increasing!

13:05.220 --> 13:07.550
Not good! Shut off the power.
Emergency stop!

13:07.550 --> 13:09.680
Abort signal transmission confirmed.

13:09.680 --> 13:11.270
It's not accepting it!

13:11.270 --> 13:12.850
The radio circuit is being blocked!

13:12.850 --> 13:14.480
It's out of control!

13:14.480 --> 13:15.640
It can't be!

13:18.270 --> 13:19.770
Run away!

13:30.120 --> 13:32.910
That robot is as badly behaved
as the guy who built it.

13:37.620 --> 13:39.130
The compression valve
is operating irregularly!

13:39.130 --> 13:40.880
The control rods aren't working!

13:40.880 --> 13:43.510
At this rate, a meltdown is possible!

13:43.510 --> 13:45.880
I don't believe it.

13:45.880 --> 13:52.510
JA's been programmed to handle
all possible contingencies.

13:52.510 --> 13:54.680
This kind of thing can't happen!

13:54.680 --> 13:58.440
Yet, the fact is, the danger of
a meltdown is now before us!

13:58.440 --> 14:02.940
Under the circumstances, our only option
is to wait for it to stop.

14:02.940 --> 14:04.490
And what is the estimated probability
of an automatic stop?

14:04.490 --> 14:08.070
0.00002%! It would be a miracle!

14:08.070 --> 14:10.530
Determined efforts are better
than waiting for a miracle!

14:10.530 --> 14:12.530
Tell me how to stop that thing!

14:12.530 --> 14:14.120
We've tried every possible option.

14:14.120 --> 14:18.920
No, there's got to be a last resort,
a way to wipe everything out.

14:18.920 --> 14:20.670
Give me the password.

14:20.670 --> 14:23.420
The password to delete all
programming is top secret.

14:23.420 --> 14:24.920
I can't authorize it.

14:24.920 --> 14:26.420
I'm not allowed to tell you!

14:26.420 --> 14:28.260
Then get the clearance!

14:28.260 --> 14:28.930
Right now!

14:30.550 --> 14:33.310
It's me. Let me speak to
Mr. Manda in Tokyo-2.

14:33.310 --> 14:36.060
That's right, the Director of Internal Affairs.

14:36.060 --> 14:39.900
Well, I've delegated this to Yasugi. Ask him.

14:41.690 --> 14:44.530
I can't give authorization for such
an important matter on the phone.

14:44.530 --> 14:47.070
Could you submit a formal written request?

14:47.070 --> 14:50.320
So, I just need to get
Mr. Yoshizawa's permission?

14:50.320 --> 14:53.200
Yes, I've already got an approval
from Mr. Witz.

14:53.200 --> 14:55.290
Yes... yes, okay.

14:55.290 --> 14:56.750
The evasion of responsibility...

14:56.750 --> 14:58.710
A written order of clearance will be sent.

14:58.710 --> 15:00.250
That will make this an official operation.

15:00.250 --> 15:04.210
We can't wait for that! Once that thing
explodes, it'll be too late!

15:08.090 --> 15:11.510
Jet Alone is heading for Atsugi.

15:11.510 --> 15:12.890
Time is running out.

15:12.890 --> 15:15.890
From here on, I'll be acting independently.

15:15.890 --> 15:17.350
Excuse me.

15:16.930 --> 15:18.430
Nerv Party

15:17.350 --> 15:18.890
Hey, Hyuga?

15:18.890 --> 15:23.440
I've arranged it with Atsugi, so bring Shinji
and Unit 01 equipped with the F module.

15:23.440 --> 15:24.980
Yes, this is an emergency.

15:24.980 --> 15:27.360
This is pointless. Call this off,
Captain Katsuragi.

15:27.360 --> 15:30.110
Besides, how do you plan to stop it?

15:30.110 --> 15:32.200
By inputting a direct command manually.

15:34.950 --> 15:36.700
Are you serious?

15:36.700 --> 15:37.660
Yes.

15:37.660 --> 15:41.290
But the interior must be
flooded with radioactivity!

15:41.290 --> 15:42.290
It's too risky!

15:42.290 --> 15:44.130
But if I make it, everyone will be saved.

15:46.590 --> 15:50.420
The hatch can be opened manually
as soon as our control signal is cut off.

15:50.420 --> 15:52.890
You'll be able to enter through the backpack.

15:54.010 --> 15:55.470
"Hope".

15:56.810 --> 15:59.020
That's the password to delete
the programming.

15:59.980 --> 16:00.930
Thank you.

16:06.110 --> 16:07.690
JA is the target.

16:07.690 --> 16:10.360
There's a danger of meltdown
within five minutes.

16:10.360 --> 16:14.870
Therefore, we cannot allow it to get
any closer to a populated area.

16:14.870 --> 16:15.490
Hyuga?

16:15.490 --> 16:16.200
Yes, Ma'am?

16:16.200 --> 16:20.370
As soon as you drop off the Eva, break away
immediately and ascend to a safe altitude.

16:20.370 --> 16:21.120
Roger.

16:21.120 --> 16:22.370
And Shinji...

16:21.750 --> 16:22.370
Yes.

16:22.370 --> 16:25.580
Run alongside the target,
and place me on its back.

16:25.580 --> 16:29.210
Then restrain the target as best you can.

16:29.210 --> 16:31.670
You're going inside?

16:31.670 --> 16:33.130
That's right.

16:33.130 --> 16:33.800
That's crazy!

16:33.800 --> 16:36.890
I know it's crazy, but there
just isn't any other way.

16:36.890 --> 16:38.720
But it's too dangerous!

16:38.720 --> 16:39.970
Don't worry.

16:39.970 --> 16:42.850
If it comes down to it, the Eva
can withstand a direct explosion.

16:42.850 --> 16:45.400
Not that! I meant for you, Miss Misato!

16:45.400 --> 16:48.400
Well, I've got to give it my best shot,

16:48.400 --> 16:50.150
or else I'll regret it for the rest of my life.

16:53.240 --> 16:54.610
Target sighted.

16:59.030 --> 17:00.330
Here we go.

17:04.960 --> 17:06.750
Eva in drop position.

17:06.750 --> 17:08.000
Docking release!

17:08.000 --> 17:08.380
Roger!

17:27.560 --> 17:28.520
We've caught up!

17:28.520 --> 17:31.110
We've got less than four minutes.
Put me on, now!

17:41.700 --> 17:43.330
That's fine! Just do it!

17:50.090 --> 17:52.170
Miss Misato!

17:55.880 --> 17:56.470
Be careful.

18:01.560 --> 18:03.180
Talk about hot.

18:03.180 --> 18:04.770
This looks bad.

18:04.770 --> 18:07.140
Stop, you bastard!

18:12.610 --> 18:14.030
Miss Misato! Hurry!

18:16.450 --> 18:17.070
This must be it.

18:30.080 --> 18:31.000
HOPE

18:32.590 --> 18:33.840
Error?

18:33.840 --> 18:35.130
What in the hell is this?

18:40.550 --> 18:43.560
There's no doubt!
The program must have been altered!

18:50.350 --> 18:53.190
The power reactor is just
0.2 short of critical!

18:53.190 --> 18:55.280
The control rods won't function!

18:55.280 --> 18:57.360
Guess it's time to sink or swim.

19:14.960 --> 19:16.920
Miss Misato, get out of there!

19:16.920 --> 19:20.010
Move, damn you!

19:24.350 --> 19:25.310
Miss Misato!

19:30.640 --> 19:32.770
0.1 to critical!

19:32.770 --> 19:34.610
It's no use! It's going to explode!

19:34.610 --> 19:35.940
It's all over.

19:35.940 --> 19:36.860
Miss Misato!

20:00.300 --> 20:01.470
She made it!

20:01.470 --> 20:02.430
Internal pressure decreasing!

20:02.430 --> 20:03.640
All readings are nominal!

20:03.640 --> 20:05.140
We're saved!

20:07.060 --> 20:09.640
We did it! We did it! We did it!

20:09.640 --> 20:11.270
That idiot.

20:11.270 --> 20:13.190
Miss Misato, are you all right?!

20:13.190 --> 20:14.230
Miss Misato?!

20:14.230 --> 20:18.110
Yeah, but I feel like crap.

20:18.110 --> 20:22.610
I'm so glad you're alive! Thank goodness!

20:22.610 --> 20:24.240
Really, thank goodness!

20:24.240 --> 20:28.950
But that was really amazing! I'm so
impressed! It really was a miracle!

20:28.950 --> 20:30.250
Yeah...

20:30.250 --> 20:33.120
But the miracle was set up by someone.

20:34.830 --> 20:37.670
Recovery of Unit 01 is complete.

20:37.670 --> 20:39.920
No danger of radioactive contamination.

20:39.920 --> 20:41.470
Except for Captain Katsuragi's actions,

20:41.470 --> 20:43.300
everything went according to plan.

20:43.300 --> 20:44.760
Good work.

20:55.060 --> 20:56.230
G'morning.

21:03.900 --> 21:06.870
Now for a morning shower!

21:06.870 --> 21:09.660
Where are my bra and panties?

21:13.000 --> 21:15.750
Good morning, Ikari!

21:15.750 --> 21:17.170
Good morning.

21:17.170 --> 21:18.630
I'm taking off!

21:18.630 --> 21:20.050
See ya!

21:21.380 --> 21:25.470
Miss Misato is just so cool!

21:25.470 --> 21:27.590
I thought so too,

21:27.590 --> 21:32.930
but at home she's shameless.
She's so coarse, uncool, and really sloppy.

21:34.230 --> 21:36.480
It makes me embarrassed for her.

21:36.480 --> 21:38.560
How nice for you.

21:40.270 --> 21:42.150
What do you mean?

21:42.150 --> 21:44.900
He really is a kid.

21:44.900 --> 21:46.150
Yeah, he sure is.

21:46.150 --> 21:47.490
How's that?

21:47.490 --> 21:51.410
She lets you see a side of her that
she won't show to anyone else.

21:51.410 --> 21:53.450
That means she's your family.

21:57.790 --> 22:00.750
TO BE CONTINUED

23:06.230 --> 23:07.150
PREVIEW

23:07.900 --> 23:13.580
Eva Unit 02 and its pilot have left
Wilhelmshaven, Germany to come to Japan!

23:13.580 --> 23:18.120
The sudden attack of an Angel forces a first
submarine battle onto the activated Unit 02!

23:18.120 --> 23:20.460
It's the next episode: "Asuka Arrives in Japan"

23:19.160 --> 23:21.210
ASUKA ARRIVES IN JAPAN
